From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: parse NVM files with an enclosing header

The WCN3991 NVM file in this phone (qca/crnv32u.bin) starts with a TLV
header of type 4 that encloses a second header of type 2, which holds
the tags. The NVM parser assumed the tags start right after the first
header, walked garbage and never found the HCI tag, so the in-band
sleep bit and the UART baud rate were never set. The file's default
rate is 3.2 Mbaud while the host runs at 3 Mbaud, so after the NVM
download the controller switched speed, the host read garbage ("Frame
reassembly failed (-84)") and HCI_RESET timed out.

Step into the inner header when the outer one has type 4, as mainline
does ("Bluetooth: qca: fix NVM configuration parsing").

---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-10-23 23:58:35.121443556 +0100
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-10-23 23:58:35.136397751 +0100
@@ -181,6 +181,16 @@
 		break;
 
 	case TLV_TYPE_NVM:
+		/* Some NVM files, such as the WCN3991 crnv32u.bin, wrap the
+		 * tags in an enclosing header of type 4, with the tags behind
+		 * a second header of type 2. Parse that set, as mainline does.
+		 */
+		if ((type_len & 0xff) == 4 && length >= sizeof(*tlv)) {
+			tlv++;
+			type_len = le32_to_cpu(tlv->type_len);
+			length = (type_len >> 8) & 0x00ffffff;
+		}
+
 		idx = 0;
 		data = tlv->data;
 		while (idx < length) {
